<h1>The 70% Rule in Wholesale Real Estate</h1>
<p class="article-lede">The 70% rule caps what you can offer on a wholesale deal: take 70% of the after repair value, subtract repairs and closing costs, then subtract your wholesale fee. What is left is your maximum allowable offer (MAO), the highest price that still leaves your end buyer their margin. On a $250,000 ARV with $30,000 of repairs, the rule gives a maximum offer of $130,000.</p>
